When investigating a different bug, I noticed that the wasm sandboxed library (graphite) compiled in tree is being compiled with incorrect flags. Per the prototype available [here](https://github.com/shravanrn/graphite_wasm/blob/master/CMakeLists.txt#L74), the wasm libraries need to be compiled with flags the specify the memory and guard page size. However, when investigating the binaries produced in the nightly Firefox 73.0a1 (2020-01-03) (64-bit), it looks like the produced binary was compiled without these flags. 

We would need to fix this as these flags are particularly important for performance, and in certain scenarios are part of the assumptions made by RLBox. 

